  "definition": "Dihydroergotamine is a drug that, in this source, was identified as a multi-targeting compound in a virtual screening study of FDA-approved drugs against multiple SARS-CoV-2 proteins. The article presents it in the context of drug repurposing and polypharmacology for possible antiviral use.",
